<description>
Repeat the populated tile pattern into every cell of a separator grid.

Input structure
- The canvas has one background color and a single non-background separator color.
- Solid separator rows and/or columns divide the canvas into equal-sized rectangular cells.
- At least one cell contains a non-background pattern, and all populated cells contain the same pattern.

Rule
- Find the separator color from the solid full-width rows or full-height columns.
- Use the separator lines to split the canvas into cells.
- Copy the unique populated cell pattern into every cell, preserving the separator lines.

Key insight
The separators define a coarse tiled board; the visible foreground pattern is the missing tile to repeat everywhere.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "foreground pattern inside the populated cell(s) of the separator grid",
  "dst": "all equal-sized cells delimited by the solid separator rows/columns",
  "transform": "copy the shared populated cell pattern into every cell while leaving separator lines unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    bg: 0 [observed]
    separator_color: any non-bg color (always 4 [observed]), forms solid full-width rows and/or full-height columns
    separator_rows: 0-2 solid rows; separator_cols: 0-2 solid columns; total separators >= 1
    cells: 2-3 row-regions x 1-3 col-regions, total cells 2-6; all cells equal size
    cell_size: 5-9 rows x 5-9 cols [observed 9x9]
    overall_grid: cell_rows * cell_h + num_sep_rows, cell_cols * cell_w + num_sep_cols
  pattern:
    location: exactly 1 cell is populated; all other cells are bg-only
    colors: 3-4 distinct non-bg, non-separator colors
    density: 8-10 non-bg pixels (~10-15% of cell area)
    no_symmetry: pattern is not LR or UD symmetric [observed]
    separator_color_absent: pattern never uses separator color
  transform:
    output copies the populated cell's pattern into every cell; separator lines unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose cell_h, cell_w in 5-9. Choose cell_rows in 2-3, cell_cols in 1-3 with total cells >= 2.
    2. Pick bg (0), separator color, and 3-4 pattern colors (all distinct, pattern colors != separator).
    3. Generate a cell_h x cell_w pattern on bg with 8-12 non-bg pixels using the pattern colors, placed randomly. Ensure no symmetry.
    4. Build output grid by tiling the pattern into all cells separated by single-pixel separator lines.
    5. Derive input by picking one random cell to keep populated; fill all other cells with bg.
```
